cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below, together with the paper."
title: "audit-horizon-core: verification code for 'Self-audit horizons of finitely axiomatized theories'"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sendo
    given-names: Hazime
    affiliation: Independent researcher, Japan
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-08
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hazime-Sendo/audit-horizon-core"
keywords:
  - finite consistency statements
  - lengths of proofs
  - singularity analysis
  - saturation audit
  - Robinson arithmetic
abstract: >-
  Python code that reproduces every numerical result of the paper "Self-audit
  horizons of finitely axiomatized theories: non-accumulation of finite
  reflection and the cost of external verification": exact formula counts and
  singularity analysis for first-order languages with terms, a linear-time
  saturation audit for fragments of Robinson's Q, and the comparison of all
  values with those printed in the paper.
references:
  - type: unpublished
    title: "Self-audit horizons of finitely axiomatized theories: non-accumulation of finite reflection and the cost of external verification"
    authors:
      - family-names: Sendo
        given-names: Hazime
    year: 2026
    notes: "Manuscript"
